id: pm-web-y80b
title: i18n plumbing + German locale for package-owned UI strings
description: Add i18n plumbing (locale catalogs + t() helper + locale resolution + language selector) and a complete German (de) locale for all package-owned UI strings in the pm-web SPA. Part of epic pm-cli-website-m1ut (German localization).
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-17T06:03:26.795Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-17T06:12:19.310Z"
assignee: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Flat JSON catalogs (en.json + de.json) cover all package-owned UI strings: auth screen, nav, banners, settings incl. registration acknowledgement, consent UI; Tiny typed t(key, params?) helper with en fallback; locale resolution localStorage.pmLocale -> navigator.language prefix match -> en; Language selector (en/Deutsch) in settings view persists choice and sets document.documentElement.lang dynamically; Dates use active locale (de-DE when de) instead of hard-coded en-US; Server API error strings stay English on the wire; translate at display layer mapping known errors to catalog keys (fallback: raw message); Legal-page localization documented as overlay-owned (operator concern); German disclaimer string present; selector does not promise translated legal pages; German translations complete and natural (Sie-Form); no visible English when de active for package-owned strings; Unit tests: locale resolution order, t() fallback + params, catalog parity (every de key exists for every en key); Functional check: auth screen renders German when localStorage.pmLocale=de"
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-17T06:12:19.310Z",pi-agent,"Implementation summary (i18n plumbing + German locale for package-owned UI strings):\n\n- Added public/src/i18n/ with en.json + de.json flat dotted-key catalogs covering all package-owned UI strings (auth screen, nav, banners, cookie-consent banner, settings incl. registration acknowledgement + language selector) plus API/OIDC error messages (mapped at the display layer) and a German legal-adjacent disclaimer string.\n- Added public/src/i18n.ts: typed t(key, params?) helper with en fallback, locale resolution (localStorage.pmLocale -> navigator.language prefix match -> en), async catalog loading via fetch, DOM binding via data-i18n/data-i18n-html/data-i18n-title/data-i18n-placeholder/data-i18n-aria attributes, document.documentElement.lang sync, translateError() display-layer mapping (fallback: raw message), and localeDate() (de-DE when de) replacing hard-coded en-US.\n- index.html: added data-i18n wiring to the auth screen, nav/top-bar, offline/install banners, and cookie-consent banner; added an inline head script to set <html lang> from localStorage.pmLocale before first paint.\n- auth.ts + settings.ts: replaced hard-coded English strings with t() calls; settings now uses localeDate() for the account-created date and exposes an en/Deutsch language selector that persists the choice and re-applies translations; API errors flow through translateError().\n- sw.ts: added /src/i18n.js, /src/i18n/en.json, /src/i18n/de.json to the service-worker precache list.\n- src/app.ts: documented that legal-page localization is overlay-owned (operator concern via PM_WEB_LEGAL_DIR) — the standalone legal HTML does not load the SPA bundle so the SPA t()/catalog plumbing cannot reach it; the language selector deliberately does not promise translated legal pages (see settings.languageHint), and a German disclaimer string (legal.disclaimer) is provided for translated legal-adjacent UI.\n\nTests added (test/i18n.test.ts): catalog parity (every en key exists in de, non-empty; no extra de keys; de differs from en for non-structural strings), locale resolution order (storage -> navigator prefix -> en; null skips a source), t()/translate fallback + {param} substitution, error.* English-value uniqueness for an unambiguous reverse map, translateError unknown-message passthrough, and a functional check simulating applyTranslations on the auth-screen block with the de catalog asserting no English auth strings remain.\n\nQuality gates: npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm test (100 passing incl. new i18n tests), npm run audit:prod, npm run pack:dry-run, and npm run changelog:check all green. German uses Sie-Form throughout."
body: ""
